§ `s 2036c(a) Annual report`

-- src:3287 | Not later than 1 year after the date specified by the Secretary during the 180-day period beginning on February 7, 2014, and annually thereafter, each State agency that carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program established under the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2011 et seq.) shall submit to the Secretary a report containing sufficient information for the Secretary to determine whether the State agency has, for the most recently concluded fiscal year preceding that annual date, verified that the State agency in that fiscal year—
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency | power: the Secretary specifies, within 180 days of February 7, 2014, the date from which the annual report falls due
-- fork: F-3 | 3286-3287 | "the 180-day period beginning on February 7, 2014": chosen reading, February 7 is the first day, so the last day is August 5, 2014; the other reading counts from February 8 and ends on August 6, 2014
@ref s 2036c(a) (src:3287)
GIVEN `the date specified by the Secretary` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A date test: TRUE from 7 February 2014 to 5 August 2014 inclusive, FALSE on 6 August 2014.
`s 2036c(a) the date specified falls within the 180-day period beginning on February 7, 2014` MEANS
    `the date specified by the Secretary` AT LEAST (Date 7 2 2014) AND `the date specified by the Secretary` AT MOST ((Date 7 2 2014) PLUS 179)

-- src:3287 | Not later than 1 year after the date specified by the Secretary during the 180-day period beginning on February 7, 2014, and annually thereafter, each State agency that carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program established under the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2011 et seq.) shall submit to the Secretary a report …
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency | claim and duty: submit the report each year, from one year after the specified date
@ref s 2036c(a) (src:3287)
GIVEN `the date specified by the Secretary` IS A DATE
      `the number of the report (1 for the first, one year after the specified date)` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the State agency submitted the report` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- A date test: the nth report is due one year after the specified date, n times over.
`s 2036c(a) the report was submitted by its due date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of the report (1 for the first, one year after the specified date)` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text counts reports from the first
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the day the State agency submitted the report` AT MOST (`add months` `the date specified by the Secretary` (12 TIMES `the number of the report (1 for the first, one year after the specified date)`)))

DECLARE `s 2036c(a) matter of the verification` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036c(a)(1) the State agency did not issue benefits to a deceased individual`
    `s 2036c(a)(2) the State agency did not issue benefits to an individual who had been permanently disqualified from receiving benefits`
    `s 2036c(a) some other matter`

-- src:3287 | a report containing sufficient information for the Secretary to determine whether the State agency has, for the most recently concluded fiscal year preceding that annual date, verified that the State agency in that fiscal year—
-- src:3288 | (1) did not issue benefits to a deceased individual; and
-- src:3289 | (2) did not issue benefits to an individual who had been permanently disqualified from receiving benefits.
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency | claim and duty: a report with enough information to determine whether it verified that it issued no benefits to a deceased or permanently disqualified individual
@ref s 2036c(a) (src:3287-3289)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 2036c(a) matter of the verification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036c(a) the report must contain sufficient information on the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 2036c(a) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists two matters and does not say they are the only ones
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3287 | each State agency that carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program established under the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2011 et seq.) shall submit to the Secretary a report containing sufficient information for the Secretary to determine whether the State agency has, for the most recently concluded fiscal year preceding that annual date, verified that the State agency in that fiscal year—
@ref s 2036c(a) (src:3287)
GIVEN `the State agency submitted the report by its due date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains sufficient information on whether the State agency issued benefits to a deceased individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report contains sufficient information on whether the State agency issued benefits to an individual who had been permanently disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- The three things subsection (a) asks of the State agency, all at once; subsection (b) turns on a failure of any of them.
`s 2036c(a) the State agency complies with subsection (a)` MEANS
    `the State agency submitted the report by its due date`
        AND `the report contains sufficient information on whether the State agency issued benefits to a deceased individual`
        AND `the report contains sufficient information on whether the State agency issued benefits to an individual who had been permanently disqualified`

§ `s 2036c(b) Penalty for noncompliance`

-- src:3291 | For any fiscal year for which a State agency fails to comply with subsection (a), the Secretary shall impose a penalty that includes a reduction of up to 50 percent of the amount that would be otherwise payable to the State agency under section 16(a) of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2025(a)) with respect to that fiscal year.
-- jural: the Secretary | a State agency that fails to comply | liability: a penalty for that fiscal year
@ref s 2036c(b) (src:3291)
GIVEN `the State agency fails to comply with subsection (a) for the fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036c(b) the Secretary must impose a penalty for the fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency fails to comply with subsection (a) for the fiscal year` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For any fiscal year for which a State agency fails to comply with subsection (a)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3291 | a penalty that includes a reduction of up to 50 percent of the amount that would be otherwise payable to the State agency under section 16(a) of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2025(a)) with respect to that fiscal year.
-- jural: a State agency | the Secretary | liability: a reduction of up to 50 percent of the amount otherwise payable under section 16(a)
@ref s 2036c(b) (src:3291)
GIVEN `the reduction, in percent of the amount otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036c(b) the reduction is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reduction, in percent of the amount otherwise payable` AT MOST 50 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reduction of up to 50 percent"

-- src:3291 | a reduction of up to 50 percent of the amount that would be otherwise payable to the State agency under section 16(a) of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2025(a)) with respect to that fiscal year.
@ref s 2036c(b) (src:3291)
GIVEN `the amount that would be otherwise payable to the State agency under section 16(a) for the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- A sum fixed by the text: 50 percent of the amount otherwise payable is the most the reduction can be.
`s 2036c(b) the largest reduction, in dollars` MEANS
    (`the amount that would be otherwise payable to the State agency under section 16(a) for the fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES 50) DIVIDED BY 100

§ `s 2036c(c) Report of pilot program to test prevention of duplicate participation`

-- src:3293 | Not later than 90 days after the completion in multiple States of a temporary pilot program to test the detection and prevention of duplicate participation by beneficiaries of the supplemental nutrition assistance program established under the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2011 et seq.), the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate …
-- jural: the Committees on Agriculture | the Secretary | claim and duty (inferred: the text names the Secretary's duty and the recipients of the report): report within 90 days of the pilot's completion
@ref s 2036c(c) (src:3293)
GIVEN `the day the pilot program was completed in multiple States` IS A DATE
      `the day the Secretary submitted the report` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test: TRUE on the 90th day after completion, FALSE on the 91st.
`s 2036c(c) the report was submitted within 90 days after the completion of the pilot program` MEANS
    `the day the Secretary submitted the report` AT MOST (`the day the pilot program was completed in multiple States` PLUS 90)

DECLARE `s 2036c(c) matter assessed by the report` IS ONE OF
    `s 2036c(c) the feasibility for the expansion of the pilot program nationwide`
    `s 2036c(c) the effectiveness for the expansion of the pilot program nationwide`
    `s 2036c(c) the cost for the expansion of the pilot program nationwide`
    `s 2036c(c) some other matter`

-- src:3293 | a report assessing the feasibility, effectiveness, and cost for the expansion of the pilot program nationwide.
@ref s 2036c(c) (src:3293)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 2036c(c) matter assessed by the report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2036c(c) the report must assess the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 2036c(c) some other matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists three matters and does not say they are the only ones
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

